{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots show the 3D French toast scene rendering properly in Chrome without errors or a blank screen.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 show orbiting and zooming around the stack, and OrbitControls sets maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.465 and maxDistance = 15.5, though screenshot 5 shows the black void edge behind the finite 34x34 tablecloth plane.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "Geometry is modest (~65k triangles total, instanced sugar, two shadow maps at 2048 and 1024) with basic EffectComposer (UnrealBloomPass + BokehPass), easily running at 30+ fps on a standard laptop after initial texture baking.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All screenshots show an on-screen UI bar at the bottom with text ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom') and interactive buttons ('Macro DoF: ON', 'Hero Angle').",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "The animate() function only updates camera controls and DoF focus distance; there is no environmental motion running on load.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 frames the French toast stack close up, slightly from above, centred on the dark plate, matching the reference photo's composition.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 clearly show three thick slices of French toast stacked and slightly rotated/offset relative to each other.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show banana slices placed between the toast layers, on top, and resting on the plate to the left and front.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show blueberries clustered on top of the stack, tucked between slices, and scattered across the foreground of the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the stack resting on a dark round ceramic plate set atop a grey-brown linen cloth.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show white specks of powdered sugar scattered over the dark plate, berries, and upper toast.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast slices have uniform scalloped, cookie-like fluted edges all the way around rather than reading as cut slices of bread with a natural rounded crust and cut edges.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show round banana discs with a faint three-pointed brownish seeded pattern in the centre.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show round blueberries of slightly varying radii with sculpted star-like calyx crowns visible on top.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 2, a blueberry under the middle slice appears suspended mid-air, and several fruit pieces clip heavily into toast slices rather than resting naturally.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2, 3, and 5 show severe rendering artifacts where transmissive syrup puddles and rivulets punch see-through holes through the banana slices and toast behind them, and screenshot 5 reveals the sharp horizon edge of the cloth against black.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the code, keyLight is positioned at (-5.2, 8.4, 5.4) (in front and left, not behind and left), and in screenshot 1 the syrup drips look dark brown rather than catching bright warm window highlights like the photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "Despite BokehPass being enabled, screenshot 1 shows almost no perceptible blur on the back rim of the plate or the cloth behind it compared to the reference photo's strong shallow depth of field.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show soft shadows grounding the plate on the cloth, the toast stack, and the fruit on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1, a solid pure-black strip is visible across the top of the frame above the tablecloth horizon.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1, the syrup drips on the toast crust read as dark, opaque-looking brown tubes without bright specular highlights, and the puddles cause sorting/transmission artifacts on nearby fruit.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast looks smooth and plastic-like with uniform pale yellow tops and striped brown fluted sides, lacking realistic caramelised uneven browning or porous cut crumb.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show blueberries with a mottled dusty slate-blue bloom texture and soft specular highlights.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1 and 4, the banana slices look flat, matte grey-beige, and suffer from dark rim/sorting artifacts rather than appearing moist and slightly translucent.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the plate with a dark ceramic sheen and subtle surface variation, and the cloth beneath has a subtle woven texture.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the plate and tablecloth sitting completely level without unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "Inspecting the code (addCrustSyrupRivulets and animate()), the syrup meshes are completely static and do not drip or move.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "There is no steam or haze system in the code or visible in any screenshot.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no environmental motion in the scene at all (animate() only updates camera controls and DoF focus).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "Although vertex displacement uses different seeds, all blueberries share the exact same UV color texture (berryTex) and all non-syrup or syrup bananas share identical color textures, making adjacent berries in screenshot 4 show identical mottled patterns.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 4 show severe clipping where banana slices on top and between layers intersect directly into the toast meshes and blueberries clip into toast and bananas.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the powdered sugar on the black plate looks like large, isolated, bright white polka dots/pellets rather than fine, soft powdered sugar.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 looks overtly stylized and synthetic—with biscuit-like scalloped toast, pellet-like white dots, clipping fruit, and UI buttons—and could not pass for the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
